(-- The time type is really a bit boguous, since, as time passes, the minimal) s
5 398 M
(-- interval between two consecutive floating-point-represented time points) s
5 390 M
(-- increases. A better approach is probably to pick a reasonable resolution) s
5 382 M
(-- and represent time and time intervals by Integer \(giving the number of) s
5 374 M
(-- "ticks"\).) s
5 358 M
(-- Time is used both for time intervals \(duration\), and time w.r.t. some) s
5 350 M
(-- agreed reference point in time. Conceptually, Time = R, i.e. time can be 0) s
5 342 M
(-- or even negative.) s
5 334 M
(type Time = Double      -- [s]) s
5 310 M
(-- DTime is the time type for lengths of sample intervals. Conceptually,) s
5 302 M
(-- DTime = R+ = { x in R | x > 0 }. Don't assume Time and DTime have the) s
5 294 M
(-- same representation.) s
5 278 M
(type DTime = Double     -- [s]) s
5 254 M
